Sure, here is a possible translation of the text into UVL-code:
```
production_line {
    type = "chocolate";
    stations {
        melting_station;
        mixing_station;
        cooling_station;
        if (type == "nut_chocolate") {
            baking_station;
        }
    };
    logistics_system;
    packaging_station;
};
```

This code defines a production line for chocolate with three mandatory stations (melting, mixing, and cooling) and an optional baking station for nut-chocolate. It also includes a logistics system and a packaging station for all types of chocolate produced on the line.